-- title:
--   Finiteness of ℚ_q generated by a finite subfield of ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $F$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ which is finite-dimensional as a $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space. Write $\iota_q =$ [`padicEmbedding q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L17) for the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q} \to$ `PadicAlgCl q` obtained by lifting along the algebraic closedness of the target (there being no canonical choice, the map is the one produced by `IsAlgClosed.lift`); here `PadicAlgCl q` is an algebraically closed field that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. The assertion is that the intermediate field of `PadicAlgCl q` over $\mathbb{Q}_q$ generated by the set-theoretic image $\iota_q(F)$, namely `IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ_[q] (padicEmbedding q '' F)`, is finite-dimensional as a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-vector space. No bound on the degree is asserted, only finiteness; in particular the statement does not claim $[\mathbb{Q}_q(\iota_q F):\mathbb{Q}_q] \le [F:\mathbb{Q}]$, although that inequality is what the proof's argument via a basis produces.
--
--   This is the basic finiteness property of the "completed level fields" $\mathbb{Q}_q(\iota_q F)$ attached, through the fixed embedding $\iota_q$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, to finite extensions $F/\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the comparison of local and global Galois groups, where the subgroups $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q(\iota_q F))$ must be seen to be open of finite index, and it is cited in particular by [`IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic`](thm.html#IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic) and by the descent step [`ExtCitation.tame_or_descent_of_isSimple`](thm.html#ExtCitation.tame_or_descent_of_isSimple).
